+++ b/packages/coding-agent/docs/rpc-attachments.md
@@ -0,0 +1,61 @@
+# Controlled attachment preparation v1
+
+This compatibility extension adds `attachment_prepare`, `attachment_cancel` and optional
+`submission_submit.preparationConsent` to the same public JSONL RPC/schema/client build. There was
+no baseline generic document-ingestion RPC. Preparation does not call prompt, ReadTool, input hooks,
+models or tools, append a message, read a browser-selected path, extract document images to disk,
+or use the shared document cache. Originals and processed representations are different objects.
+
+Preparation takes an ordered draft revision, authority generation, unchanged native prose, and
+controlled `{originalId,format,sha256,data}` objects. It returns every item's actual failure or staged
+text/image representation, degradation codes and structured native facts (dimensions/frame/decoded allocation,
+converted bytes, PDF OCR pages/encoding, embedded image omissions), a versioned binding and an expiring digest. Any failed
+item prevents consumption of the entire input. Truncation, document structure loss, omitted images/
+PDF text and first-frame animation loss require explicit acceptance of that result. Names are
+presentation data outside this interface; no filename becomes `@path` or an extraction destination.
+Native manual `@path`, slash commands and templates retain their own meaning.
+
+Protected native source/instance/Session, history context, model/thinking/tool context, draft,
+object identity/order/content, authority generation and budget version fence the receipt. The Host
+must also check authentication/current grants at each intake/read/consumption. Opaque generations
+and content hashes grant no original or filesystem access. Cancellation invalidates pending
+publication and ready receipts; restart requires fresh preparation. Stale or partially ready input
+never silently becomes text-only input.
+
+Consumption freezes the exact staged wire fields while permitting native internal cache annotations, then #36 durably reserves its stable client submission
+identity before input dispatch. Explicit causal original/prepared identities travel on actual native
+user/companion objects. Consumption never rereads a path or reconverts an original. Durable duplicate
+lookup precedes ephemeral receipt validation, so receipt loss cannot cause replay. Query distinguishes
+reserved originals from actual committed entry relations: reservation/acknowledgement alone is not
+a Sent Attachment. `attachment-provenance-v1` is a native required feature; older compatibility
+readers must refuse rather than rewrite away metadata they do not understand.
+
+Persisted entry relations may include `entryPart: {kind: "content" | "files", index}`. This zero-based
+index addresses the actual saved native body: an image's `content` part or a converted document's
+`files` item, with indices bounded to 0–65535. Native staging retains the exact part's object identity;
+the final message construction locates it after filtering and reordering. Equal bytes, an original
+hash, a planned position or a replacement object cannot establish that association. Removed,
+changed or duplicated parts instead carry `entryPartUnavailable: "missing" | "changed" | "ambiguous"`.
+Reservation manifests have no persisted slot. A locator proves the saved representation's causal
+position; it does not establish provider delivery or grant access to the Host-owned original.
+
+Converters use an owned Linux process, synthetic home, allowlisted environment, pre-import network
+denial, 512 MiB data/eight CPU-second ceilings, ten wall seconds, bounded output and kill/reap.
+Missing containment/converters refuse preparation. Raw limits remain 10 MiB/image, 5 MiB/text/document,
+eight objects and 32 MiB/input. Decoded images allow 16,777,216 pixels/64 MiB RGBA, including declared
+animation frames; 16-bit PNG allocation is charged at eight bytes/pixel and GIF frames must fit their canvas.
+Office packages require the selected main content type, and unsupported XML encodings fail instead of being replaced.
+Prepared images fit 1568 pixels/500 KiB and avoid WebP; inline text fits 3000 lines/
+50 KiB after at most 2 MiB conversion output. ZIP limits are 2048 members, 512 KiB index, 8 MiB/member,
+32 MiB expansion and 1024 path bytes. Preparation has sixty seconds; two receipts/16 MiB are staged
+for five minutes. Processed receipt/model data has a separate 8 MiB limit.
+
+The advertised `bounded-jsonl-input-v1` policy keeps stdin unchunked and caps complete JSONL commands,
+including base64, escapes, metadata and newline, at 48 MiB. UTF-8 is fatal. Malformed input, oversize
+lines and partial EOF produce fixed sanitized errors. Startup holds at most eight frames/48 MiB;
+the dispatcher retains at most 32 frames/64 MiB. Strict-start's earlier control/handoff limits remain
+separate. Stdout retains its independent 1 MiB physical/64 MiB negotiated reassembly limits;
+preparation replies additionally cap logical/physical aggregate bytes at 9/12 MiB.
+
+Private product Session admission remains blocked. Native data/fault, Host/DSH/browser, rollback
+and the final matched artifact gates remain independent from isolated preparation/source checks.
